<title>ITALY: Italian Aug wage inflation 4.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Italian Aug wage inflation 4.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian wage inflation stood at an annual 4.4 percent in August, statistics institute ISTAT said in a statement.</p>
<p>ITALIAN HOURLY WAGE INFLATION</p>
<p>				   Aug 1996     July 1996</p>
<p> Year/year change		4.4%	   +3.9%</p>
<p> Month/month change	    0.5%	   +0.7%</p>
<p> Index (base 1995=100)     102.8	   102.3</p>
<p>Istat said wage inflation in the agriculture sector rose 0.4 percent year-on-year in August, 3.4 percent in the industrial sector, 4.6 percent in the chemical sector, 3.7 percent in the metal workers sector, 2.7 percent in the service sector and 2.4 percent in the transport and communications sector.</p>
<p>The statistics office added that the number of hours lost to industrial action in the first seven months of 1996 was a provisional 2.1 million hours from 4.2 million.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
